":"MPH — Biostatistics"},{"text":"Health Data Science"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MPH"},{"text":"M.Sc Public Health"},{"text":"Community Medicine/public-health-related programs where eligible"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Research"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Clinical Research"},{"text":"Public Health Research"},{"text":"Health Informatics"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For a student specifically targeting Epidemiologist, an MPH/M.Sc Epidemiology is one of the strongest next steps."},{"type":"h","text":"Career Specializations"},{"type":"h","text":"Infectious Disease Epidemiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Outbreaks"},{"text":"Communicable diseases"},{"text":"Surveillance"},{"text":"Transmission dynamics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Non-Communicable Disease Epidemiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Diabetes"},{"text":"Cardiovascular disease"},{"text":"Cancer"},{"text":"Hypertension"},{"text":"Population risk factors"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Hospital Epidemiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Healthcare-associated infections"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Antimicrobial resistance"},{"text":"Hospital surveillance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Environmental Epidemiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Study relationships between:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Air pollution"},{"text":"Water quality"},{"text":"Climate"},{"text":"Environmental exposures"},{"text":"Health outcomes"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Occupational Epidemiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Workplace exposures"},{"text":"Occupational diseases"},{"text":"Injury surveillance"},{"text":"Worker health"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Digital Epidemiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Real-time health data"},{"text":"Digital surveillance"},{"text":"Mobility data"},{"text":"Online signals"},{"text":"AI-assisted outbreak detection"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"BPH / B.Sc Public Health"},{"type":"h","text":"Epidemiology Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Epidemiology / Surveillance Analyst"},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"Epidemiologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Epidemiologist / Disease Surveillance Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health Program / Research Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health Leadership"},{"type":"h","text":"A data-oriented pathway can develop as:"},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health Graduate"},{"type":"h","text":"Health Data Assistant"},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health Data Analyst"},{"type":"h","text":"Epidemiological Data Analyst"},{"type":"h","text":"Health Data Scientist"},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health Analytics Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"Recommended Final Skill Stack"},{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should aim for:"},{"type":"h","text":"Epidemiology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Incidence"},{"text":"Prevalence"},{"text":"Risk measures"},{"text":"Study designs"},{"text":"Bias"},{"text":"Confounding"},{"text":"Causal reasoning"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Statistics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Descriptive statistics"},{"text":"Inferential statistics"},{"text":"Regression"},{"text":"Confidence intervals"},{"text":"Statistical interpretation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Data"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Excel"},{"text":"SQL"},{"text":"R/Python"},{"text":"Power BI"},{"text":"Data cleaning"},{"text":"Data visualization"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Public Health"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Disease surveillance"},{"text":"Outbreak investigation"},{"text":"Field epidemiology"},{"text":"Health programs"},{"text":"Research methodology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Health informatics"},{"text":"AI-assisted surveillance"},{"text":"Predictive analytics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Target Profile by Graduation"},{"type":"p","text":"Public Health graduate with strong foundations in epidemiology and biostatistics, practical experience in disease surveillance and public-health research, proficiency in health-data cleaning and visualization, exposure to outbreak-investigation methodology, and working knowledge of Excel, SQL, R/Python, Power BI, and basic GIS."},{"type":"h","text":"Best Overall Positioning"},{"type":"flow","items":["Public Health","Epidemiology","Biostatistics","Disease Surveillance","Health Data Analytics","Research Methods","GIS"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"This pathway is particularly suitable for students interested in disease surveillance, public-health research, population health, health analytics, outbreak investigation, and evidence-based health programs."},{"type":"note","label":"Database note","text":"“Epidemiology Assistant” is a suitable entry-level target career for BPH/B.Sc Public Health. For database progression, distinguish it from Epidemiologist, which typically requires postgraduate epidemiology/public-health training and relevant experience."}]}]}